It is Saturday afternoon.
I am resting in the flat.
Suddenly I hear a sound from the bedroom.
I go there.
There I see him.
Moti is chewing one of my shoes!
He is chewing it very happily.
I clap my hands.
I say loudly, "Moti, no!"
"Drop it!"
"Give it to me immediately!"
He looks at me, but does not drop the shoe.
I quickly bring his toy.
I call him, "Moti, come here."
"Look at this toy, take it."
"Chewing shoes must not be done!"
He drops the shoe and takes the toy.
I look at my shoe.
It is a little wet, but safe.
